<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49695" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">umbrācŭlum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		umbra (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>any thing that furnishes shade</i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a shady place</i>,
				<i>bower</i>, <i>arbor</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 51, 2</span></i>; Cic. Fragm. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 6, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 9,
				42</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a school</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in solem et pulverem, ut e Theophrasti
					doctissimi hominis umbraculis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 9, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex umbraculis eruditorum in solem atque in
					pulverem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Leg. 3, 6, 14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A sunshade</i>, <i>parasol</i>, <i>umbrella</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2,
				311</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. A. 2, 209</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 14,
				28, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tib. 2, 5, 97</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 315, 16</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
